= <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> Moderates split!

The moderate anti-Mallin wing of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> had already decided to break with the party, and it was only a matter of finding the right pretext. This opportunity came when Mallin passed a resolution to strengthen his <i>principle of absolute leadership</i> over the party, making the decisions of the party executive committee and leader binding on all members of the party’s delegations to the Assembly and state parliaments.

The moderates within the party were powerless to stop the adoption of the resolution, which led to Westmore and the remaining moderates [? if not kvp_formed: splitting off into various parties on the moderate Commonwealth right?][? if kvp_formed: to join their friends in the newly founded <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span>?].

- @dnvp_split: About time.


@dnvp_split
on-arrival: other_r += traditionalist_r*0.3 if not kvp_formed; kvp_r += traditionalist_r*0.3 if kvp_formed; traditionalist_r = traditionalist_r*0.7; landed_traditionalist -= 4; burgher_traditionalist -= 4; guild_traditionalist -= 4; landed_other += 4 if not kvp_formed; burgher_other += 4 if not kvp_formed; guild_other += 4 if not kvp_formed; landed_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; burgher_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; guild_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; traditionalist_split_2 = 1; traditionalist_split_2_timer = 1 if not kvp_formed
face-image: img/portraits/Kuno_von_Westarp.jpg

Unfortunately, the party district organizations remain loyal to Mallin, who has worked to fill the party bureaucracy with his own supporters. As a result, the defection of the entire moderate wing of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> is less impactful than it would have been. Furthermore, many on the right believe that an internal resolution is not a strong enough pretext to break with the party and may choose to remain with Mallin.